+        if (!bytes.empty()) transport.MarkBytesSent(provider.ConsumeIntegralInRange<size_t>(0, bytes.size()));
+    }
+    transport.GetInfo();

comments.body:
The target calls `transport.GetInfo()` and drops the result.

The transport reports v2 once it verifies the version packet:
https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/a773e1e33b349dc819b5a0edc1c7a4839dc73b48/src/net.cpp#L1595-L1600

At that point its session id should match the peer's. Would an assert on that work? I ran the check for 4 minutes and it didn't fail.


```suggestion
    const auto info{transport.GetInfo()};
    if (info.transport_type == TransportProtocolType::V2) {
        assert(info.session_id == uint256{MakeUCharSpan(peer.GetSessionID())});
    }
```

